# All variables below are optional. With nothing set, the app runs fully
# offline on the built-in mock STT + mock analysis providers — zero signups,
# zero cost. Fill these in only when you want real transcription/translation.

# --- Speech-to-text (pick one; both have free tiers, no card required) ---
# STT_PROVIDER=amivoice          # or "speechmatics" / "mock" — auto-detected from keys below if unset
# AMIVOICE_API_KEY=              # https://amivoice.com — 60 min/month free
# SPEECHMATICS_API_KEY=          # https://portal.speechmatics.com — free trial credit
# SPEECHMATICS_REGION=eu1

# --- Translation / analysis ---
# LLM_PROVIDER=gemini            # or "mock" — auto-detected from GEMINI_API_KEY if unset
# GEMINI_API_KEY=                # https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# GEMINI_MODEL=gemini-flash-lite-latest
#
# The free tier caps out at a very small number of requests/day per model
# (as low as ~20/day as of 2026) — fine to try the app, but real use (long
# recordings especially) needs billing enabled on the underlying Google
# Cloud project for pay-as-you-go rate limits. Same API key either way, no
# key rotation needed. Current pricing: https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/pricing
#
# NEXT_PUBLIC_GEMINI_BUDGET_JPY=2000
#
# Optional: shows a progress bar in the sidebar against a known prepaid
# balance (e.g. what you actually topped up), alongside the cost estimate
# that's always shown once any session has real usage. Unlike every other
# variable on this page, this one is baked into the app at BUILD time (the
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix is what exposes it to the browser) — set it before
# deploying/rebuilding, not just at runtime, or it won't take effect until
# the next build.

# --- Persistence ---
# FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
# FIREBASE_CLIENT_EMAIL=
# FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY=
#
# When all three are set, sessions/reports are saved to Firestore and
# survive restarts/redeploys, and the sidebar loads your history on page
# load. Unset by default — falls back to an in-memory store (current
# behavior: history lives only as long as the server process, gone on any
# restart or redeploy). Audio itself is never persisted either way — only
# the transcript/translation/report.
#
# From Firebase Console -> Project Settings -> Service Accounts -> Generate
# new private key (downloads a JSON file with these three values).
# FIREBASE_PRIVATE_KEY normally has real newlines, which most env var UIs
# (Render included) don't reliably preserve in a single-line field — paste
# it with literal \n sequences instead (e.g. "-----BEGIN...\nMIIEv...\n...");
# the app unescapes them automatically. Firestore's free (Spark) tier is
# plenty for personal use, no card required.

# --- Access control ---
# APP_PASSWORD=
#
# When set, the whole app (including /api/sessions, so real STT/Gemini
# calls can't be triggered by a stranger who finds the URL) requires this
# password. Unset by default — the app is fully public, matching every
# other feature's "works with zero config" default. Set this once real
# money is on the line (a paid Gemini/Speechmatics plan).
